WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.540
Hey guys, this is Donia Duchess,

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:03.470
and this is the 2020 Census explained

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:06.887
by puppies, kittens, and a pregnant lady!

00:00:16.399 --> 00:00:17.612
Come here!

00:00:18.546 --> 00:00:19.379
Look at that!

00:00:19.379 --> 00:00:20.212
Come here!

00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:21.690
Oh my god!

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:24.640
This is gonna be way
too much fun, you guys.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:25.577
Thanks, buddy!

00:00:25.577 --> 00:00:28.077
"This year, you can
complete the 2020 Census

00:00:28.077 --> 00:00:30.310
"online- or by phone, or by mail."

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.143
That's great.

00:00:31.143 --> 00:00:33.150
This is the first year
that it's available online.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:34.660
Which makes it easy for
me, 'cause I can sit here

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.297
and play with the puppies
as much as I want.

00:00:36.297 --> 00:00:38.037
"College students who live away from home

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:41.277
"should be counted at the
on or off-campus residence

00:00:41.277 --> 00:00:45.027
"where they live and
sleep most of the time."

00:00:48.527 --> 00:00:51.347
"The 2020 Census will
inform how we spend hundreds

00:00:51.347 --> 00:00:54.247
"of billions of dollars in
federal funds every year.

00:00:54.247 --> 00:00:56.707
"Pet stores can use 2020 Census data

00:00:56.707 --> 00:00:59.170
"to help decide where to put new stores."

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:01.126
They like the facts!

00:01:01.126 --> 00:01:02.860
Oh my God!

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:03.747
"One of the things

00:01:03.747 --> 00:01:06.850
"census data will help inform
is where to build new roads."

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:08.934
Hey, fresh concrete!

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:09.877
Thank you!

00:01:09.877 --> 00:01:12.997
"The census never asks for Social Security

00:01:12.997 --> 00:01:14.117
"or credit card numbers."

00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:15.340
So that means your stuff

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.280
is protected, okay?

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.042
Oh my god, it's happening.

00:01:19.042 --> 00:01:20.447
Oh!

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:24.067
"The 2020 Census doesn't
count pets," aw, man!

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.617
"But it does count everyone living

00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:29.417
"in the 50 states, DC,
and five U.S. territories.

00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:31.487
"Even newborn babies need to be counted,

00:01:31.487 --> 00:01:33.517
"even if they're still in the hospital.

00:01:33.517 --> 00:01:35.591
"The census determines how many seats

00:01:35.591 --> 00:01:36.424
"in the House

00:01:36.424 --> 00:01:38.420
"of Representatives each state gets."

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.253
Good thing to know!

00:01:39.253 --> 00:01:40.963
Will you help me get one?

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:44.100
This is harder than I thought!

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.690
Wait, oof, okay.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:48.126
All right, this is happening, go for it.

00:01:48.126 --> 00:01:48.959
Ha!

00:01:48.959 --> 00:01:51.357
"The results of the
2020 Census will inform

00:01:51.357 --> 00:01:53.917
"how billions of dollars
in federal funding

00:01:53.917 --> 00:01:55.937
"are allocated to many programs,

00:01:55.937 --> 00:01:58.487
"including Medicaid, Head Start, grants

00:01:58.487 --> 00:02:01.090
"for mental health
services, and so much more."

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:02.783
Thank you for that!

00:02:02.783 --> 00:02:06.017
"The U.S. Census Bureau
is bound by law to protect

00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:09.730
"your answers and keep them
strictly confidential."

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:11.377
Did you give me a fact?

00:02:11.377 --> 00:02:14.640
"It's important to count all
your roommates on the census."

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:15.670
And there you have it.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.920
Make sure you complete the 2020 Census.

